## Local environment and Vercel

The Vue/Vite frontend reads `VITE_API_URL` from its root `.env.local`; locally it
defaults to `http://localhost:3000`. Set it to the deployed API base URL in the
Vercel frontend project's environment settings for Preview and Production.

The Next.js API server reads `CLOUDINARY_CLOUD_NAME`, `CLOUDINARY_API_KEY`,
`CLOUDINARY_API_SECRET`, and `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGIN` from `api-server/.env.local`
for local development. Configure those values in the API project's Vercel
environment settings as server-only variables. `CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGIN` must be
the exact frontend origin for the respective Preview or Production environment.
Use `.env.example` and `api-server/.env.example` as variable-name references;
never put real credentials in either example file or source control.